🇮🇷🇺🇸🇨🇳US Blockade of Iran = Distant Blockade of China 

▪️Iran appears to be admitting/confirming information that the US blockade has significantly reduced Iranian energy exports (which primarily go to China);  

▪️Iran's plans to "break" the blockade imply it isn't already circumventing it, and coincide with Western media reports that Iranian energy exports are low to entirely cut; 

▪️Iran's PressTV repeats claims Iran will target energy infrastructure across West Asia if its efforts to break the US blockade are thwarted - however this will only enhance US efforts to cut Asia off from West Asian energy exports; 

▪️In previous analysis I pointed out how the US blockade was viable and together with its wider war - was cutting off energy exports to both China and the rest of Asia as a core objective of US war on Iran and part of the US' wider war on multipolarism; 

▪️Conversely, China has spent decades preparing for this eventuality - the question is - did it prepare enough;
